      answer: "c",
      explanation: "Ethylene is the methionine-derived gaseous plant hormone associated with fruit ripening, and its structure is H2C=CH2. The source heading incorrectly draws HC triple-bond CH, which is acetylene, not ethylene. Ethane and methane are also hydrocarbons, but they are not the ripening hormone identified in this pathway.",
      sectionId: "ethylene-chemistry-and-effects", source: { document: "biology", page: 301 }, cognitive: "recall"
