      answer: "d",
      explanation: "Greater growth of the upper side makes that side longer and bends the organ downward, the defining relationship of epinasty. Hyponasty has the reverse upper-versus-lower relationship and produces upward curvature. Thermotaxis concerns locomotion along temperature gradients, and diageotropism concerns a growth orientation approximately perpendicular to gravity, neither of which is specified here.",
      sectionId: "epinasty-hyponasty-and-nutation", source: { document: "biology", page: 308 }, cognitive: "understanding"
