      answer: "b",
      explanation: "Free searching or circling of a growing tendril is endogenous nutation or circumnutation. Contact with a support supplies an external directional stimulus, and the subsequent growth response is thigmotropism or haptotropism. The source specifically distinguishes the unsupported tendril from the contacted one, so both movements should not be assigned the same cause merely because the same organ performs them.",
      sectionId: "epinasty-hyponasty-and-nutation", source: { document: "biology", page: 308 }, cognitive: "application"
